Subject: [PATCH 128/155] [ae-patch] Predict the next prompt in every session,
 on named Claude accounts and in Codex

The side call that 0123 added now serves every session. A Claude session on a
named account (its bridge dir's claude_account names one) calls on that
account's token, resolved with claude_accounts.account_env exactly as the
terminal launch resolves it and passed only as CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN in the
call's environment; an empty file keeps the default login and a name that
cannot be resolved skips. The Codex forwarder notes each turn's userMessage and
agentMessage and, on the live turn/completed that posts the idle edge, makes
the same call on the host's active Claude account, with the same skips, cancel,
clear and external_session_suggestion event. The shared parts moved to
harnesses/ae_prompt_suggest_core.py.
